<title>USA: U.S. interest rates higher in latest week.</title>
<headline>U.S. interest rates higher in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve announced average interest rates for the week ended March 7, compared with the Feb 28 week, as follows:</p>
<p>   Federal funds rate.................5.36 vs 5.16</p>
<p>   3-month Treasury bills.............5.09 vs 5.05</p>
<p>   3-month commercial paper...........5.46 vs 5.40</p>
<p>   3-month bankers acceptances........5.35 vs 5.28</p>
<p>   3-month CDs........................5.44 vs 5.37</p>
<p>   3-month Eurodollar.................5.44 vs 5.34</p>
<p>   30-year Government bond............6.85 vs 6.75</p>
</text>
